                <pb facs="0356" n="248" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg248"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163/100: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-22T10:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 22,
                                1927—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 23—11:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>60. Following from American consul at Foochow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“January 20, 5 p.m.</p>
                        <list>
                            <label>1.</label>
                            <item>Reports from sources so authenticated and friendly as to be
                                credible indicate the probability further attacks upon foreign
                                mission property within a few days. When the <hi rendition="#italic"
                                    >Pillsbury</hi> left here yesterday afternoon she expected that
                                another vessel would be sent to Foochow shortly. Can you confirm the
                                arrangement as I have not had any further information or any word
                                from the <hi rendition="#italic">Pillsbury?</hi></item>
                            <label>2.</label>
                            <item>The evacuation Americans is progressing.”</item>
                        </list>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Commander in chief has informed me that <hi rendition="#italic">Parrott</hi> is
                    proceeding Foochow to replace <hi rendition="#italic">Pillsbury</hi>.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
